<header><p class="enc-kicker">Place · city</p><h1 class="enc-title">Shillong</h1></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Shillong is a hill city in north-eastern <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/india">India</a> and the capital of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/meghalaya">Meghalaya</a>. Founded as a British station in the 1860s on the lands of the Khasi state of Mylliem, it became the capital of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/assam">Assam</a> in 1874 and remained so until Meghalaya was formed in 1972. Its cool climate and pine-covered hills earned it the name '<a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/scotland">Scotland</a> of the East'.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/shillong.jpg" alt="Shillong" width="320" height="205" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: Prasanta Kr Dutta · CC BY-SA 4.0 · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Elephant_Falls_II,_Shillong.jpg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
